<%# One row of the §7.1 two-filter bar. Locals: label, param, current, values
    ([value, text] pairs) and base_params (the currently active pair, so flipping
    one filter never resets the other).

    Plain links, not a JS-driven control: the whole filter state is two query
    params, which makes it bookmarkable, back-button-correct and directly
    assertable in a request spec — and Turbo Drive already makes it feel local.
    The anchor keeps the catalogue in view instead of jumping to the page top.

    Shape: the row of segments (F9 of the surface table), one value of several, the
    chosen one tinted with an ink edge and a check. No black fill: that read as the
    loudest thing on the page for what is a quiet narrowing. %>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
  <span class="text-sm text-muted md:w-32 shrink-0"><%= label %></span>
  <div class="inline-flex flex-wrap">
    <% values.each do |value, text| %>
      <% active = current == value %>
      <%= link_to organisation_ai_settings_path(@organisation,
                                                base_params.merge(param => value, anchor: 'ai_packages')),
                  class: "relative -ml-px inline-flex h-8 items-center gap-1.5 border px-4 text-sm first:ml-0 first:rounded-l-md last:rounded-r-md #{
                    active ? 'z-10 border-ink bg-cream-200 font-semibold text-heading'
                           : 'border-cream-300 bg-surface-raised text-body hover:bg-cream-100'
                  }",
                  aria: { current: active ? 'true' : nil } do %>
        <% if active %><i class="bi bi-check2" aria-hidden="true"></i><% end %><%= text %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
